# Chkela study notes

Use when creating/editing CMS notes (`shared/content/data.json` → sync `assets/content/data.json`).

## Goal

Fast, exam-ready revision. Voice: clear student coach. Notes must cover the textbook **learning competencies** for that chapter.

## Competency coverage (required)

1. Copy the chapter **Content / Learning competencies** from the MoE unit opener into the chapter overview (`callout exam`).
2. Map every competency to at least one lesson note. If a competency is missing, add or expand a lesson.
3. Lesson notes teach what students must **do** (define, state, classify, describe, list, argue).

## Classification

- Lessons first, then **one note per lesson** (`lessonId`).
- **Overview + Summary only** on `Chapter overview & summary` (`order: 0`).
- Lesson notes: that section only. No per-lesson Overview/Summary.

## No-dash writing (required)

Never use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`). Prefer periods, colons, or parentheses. No "Term — definition" bullets.

## Engaging markup

```html
<div class="section-label">2.1</div>
<h2>Characteristics of living things</h2>
<p class="lead">Hook in one plain sentence.</p>
<p>Use <span class="hl">highlights</span> and <span class="u">underlines</span> on key phrases.</p>
<div class="key-term"><span class="kt-label">Key term</span><strong class="u">Taxonomy.</strong> Definition here.</div>
<ul class="note-list"><li>…</li></ul>
<div class="callout tip"><span class="callout-label">Exam tip</span><p>…</p></div>
```

Highlight: `hl`, `hl-pink`, `hl-mint`. Underline: `u`, `u-wavy`, `u-double`.

Chapter overview: `note-hero`, competencies in `callout exam`, `summary-box`.

Math: `$inline$` / `$$display$$`. Sync `assets/content/data.json` after edits.
